# Eleventy's input directory is `docs/`, and its output directory is inside it. Both of
# those need saying out loud here, because the alternative is a build that renders its own
# output and grows a copy of every page on each run.
docs/site

# The standalone pages: three generated HTML libraries that are whole documents with their
# own <head>, their own theme toggle and their own module imports. They are served from
# `docs/` directly — `server.cjs` falls back there for anything not in `docs/site` — so
# they need no layout wrapped round them and would be broken by one.
docs/*.html

# Imagery, linked by the built pages rather than copied into them. Kept out of the build
# so 5MB of PNGs are not walked on every run; the deploy recipes ship `docs/images` whole.
docs/images

# The sidebar is a plain module rather than an Eleventy data file, so that the config and
# the directory data files can both import it. Eleventy ignores unknown extensions anyway;
# this is belt and braces.
docs/_nav.mjs

